.TH RECVFROM 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
recvfrom \- receive bytes and optionally a source address
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B ssize_t recvfrom(int descriptor, void* buffer, size_t length, int flags,
.B                  struct sockaddr* address, socklen_t* address_length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives up to length bytes. The buffer must be writable and large enough.
When address is supplied, address_length supplies its capacity and receives
the actual address length. Pass NULL for both to omit the address.
Flags include MSG_PEEK and MSG_DONTWAIT; Linux receive semantics apply.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the byte count, possibly short, or \-1 with errno set.
Zero can indicate end of stream. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recvmsg (3crunch),
.BR recvfrom (2)
